1
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:01,660
Thorndyke's.

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:04,240
Good morning. Is that Mr Thorndyke?

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:06,260
Speaking. How can I help?

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:08,620
I've got quite a few things

5
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,080
which need painting and fixing in the flat

6
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,820
and I wonder whether you'd be able to do the work.

7
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,460
I'm sure I'd be able to help but let me take down a few details.

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,000
Yes, of course.

9
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:22,640
Well, firstly, how did you hear about us?

10
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,160
It was my friend May Hampton

11
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:29,540
you did some excellent work for her a couple of years ago. Do you remember?

12
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,800
Oh, yes, that was in West Park Flats, lovely lady.

13
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,100
Yes, she is.

14
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,260
And what's your name, please?

15
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,290
It's Edith Pargetter.

16
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:43,200
Edith... can you spell your surname, please?

17
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:49,040
It's P-A-R-G-E-double T-E-R.

18
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:53,640
Double T, right. And do you live in West Park Flats as well?

19
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,560
No, actually it's East Park, Flat 4.

20
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:03,120
Oh, right, that's over the road, I seem to remember - quite difficult to get to.

21
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,920
Yes. it's at the back of the library.

22
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,480
Right, I know. And what's your phone number?

23
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,940
875934 but I'm out a great deal in the afternoons and evenings.

24
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:20,380
So would the best time to ring you be in the morning?

25
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:21,160
Yes.

26
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:23,940
Fine. I've made a note of that.

27
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:26,420
Can I just ask, I'll be in a van

28
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:29,220
and I know parking's rather difficult round your flats.

29
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,080
Where would you recommend?

30
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:39,220
Well, I always tell people in larger vehicles to park by the post box on the other side of the road from the entrance.

31
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:40,900
Good, thanks.

32
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:44,900
And will you be able to give me a full itemised quote?

33
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:49,140
Oh. Yes, I'll list all the jobs separately with individual prices.

34
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:50,900
That'd be a great help.

35
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:51,740
No problem.

36
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,620
Now, what would you like me to do?

37
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:59,560
Firstly and most urgently is in the kitchen.

38
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,500
With all the weather damage

39
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:05,280
the glass in the door has cracked and I'd need that fixing...

40
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,580
I presume you mean replacing?

41
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,400
Oh, yes. And as soon as possible...

42
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,020
What I'll do is come round tomorrow morning and do that immediately.

43
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:18,900
Thank you so much. The other things aren't so urgent but...

44
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,700
Now, I'll make a note of everything you want doing.

45
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:25,960
Well, in the kitchen I'd like some painting doing.

46
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,800
All the kitchen walls?

47
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:31,800
Just the area over the cooker. It's very greasy...

48
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,280
Right... it does tend to get that way!

49
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:35,160
Yes!

50
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:40,160
Well, if you want a proper job done what I'd need to do is strip the old paint

51
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,880
and plaster it about a week before I paint it.

52
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:47,840
Of course. Now, May tells me you also do work in the garden.

53
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,160
That's right.

54
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:52,180
Well. I'd like you to replace a fence.

55
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,460
Just one?

56
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,600
Yes, at the far end.

57
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,260
Fine. Shouldn't be a problem.

58
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:58,920
And that's the lot.

59
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:04,200
Fine. Yeah, as I say I can come round tomorrow morning to look over things with you.

60
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:05,960
That's great, thank you.

61
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,860
So, I'll look forward to seeing you tomorrow at...
